",\"relative\":\"!4180\",\"full\":\"root/openhands!4180\"},\"web_url\":\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/merge_requests/4180\",\"time_stats\":{\"time_estimate\":0,\"total_time_spent\":0,\"human_time_estimate\":null,\"human_total_time_spent\":null},\"squash\":false,\"squash_on_merge\":false,\"task_completion_status\":{\"count\":1,\"completed_count\":1},\"has_conflicts\":false,\"blocking_discussions_resolved\":true},{\"id\":12759,\"iid\":4179,\"project_id\":9,\"title\":\"Enable authentication for runtime environments\",\"description\":\"*Created by: rbren*\\\\n\\\\n**End-user friendly description of the problem this fixes or functionality that this introduces**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- [ ] Include this change in the Release Notes. If checked, you must provide an **end-user friendly** description for your change below\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNo release notes needed\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n---\\\\r\\\\n**Give a summary of what the PR does, explaining any non-trivial design decisions**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf the remote runtime returns a `session_api_key`, the client will now always check that key before allowing any meaningful endpoints to be hit.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTested this using the eval remote runtime\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n---\\\\r\\\\n**Link of any specific issues this addresses**\\\\r\\\\n\",\"state\":\"opened\",\"created_at\":\"2024-10-02T20:16:07.000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-02T20:16:11.000Z\",\"merged_by\":null,\"merge_user\":null,\"merged_at\":null,\"closed_by\":null,\"closed_at\":null,\"target_branch\":\"main\",\"source_branch\":\"rb/session-keys\",\"user_notes_count\":1,\"upvotes\":0,\"downvotes\":0,\"author\":{\"id\":1,\"username\":\"root\",\"name\":\"Administrator\",\"state\":\"active\",\"locked\":false,\"avatar_url\":\"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/bc780a96456fadbe364f4d9b9ef1276c288db81171546a91d8331887c81b9cf3?s=80\\\\u0026d=identicon\",\"web_url\":\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root\"},\"assignees\":[],\"assignee\":null,\"reviewers\":[],\"source_project_id\":9,\"target_project_id\":9,\"labels\":[],\"draft\":false,\"imported\":true,\"imported_from\":\"gitlab_project\",\"work_in_progress\":false,\"milestone\":null,\"merge_when_pipeline_succeeds\":false,\"merge_status\":\"unchecked\",\"detailed_merge_status\":\"unchecked\",\"merge_after\":null,\"sha\":\"3f35dd267e42cfda4fbe03698165d86d02d19782\",\"merge_commit_sha\":null,\"squash_commit_sha\":null,\"discussion_locked\":null,\"should_remove_source_branch\":null,\"force_remove_source_branch\":null,\"prepared_at\":null,\"reference\":\"!4179\",\"references\":{\"short\":\"!4179\",\"relative\":\"!4179\",\"full\":\"root/openhands!4179\"},\"web_url\":\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/merge_requests/4179\",\"time_stats\":{\"time_estimate\":0,\"total_time_spent\":0,\"human_time_estimate\":null,\"human_total_time_spent\":null},\"squash\":false,\"squash_on_merge\":false,\"task_completion_status\":{\"count\":1,\"completed_count\":0},\"has_conflicts\":false,\"blocking_discussions_resolved\":true},{\"id\":40494,\"iid\":9590,\"project_id\":14,\"title\":\"[Discussion] Thoughts on this pattern for WidgetLabel / Toolbar?\",\"description\":\"*Created by: sfc-gh-nbellante*\\\\n\\\\n# Description\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIn the process of investigating migrating remaining components to utilize the \\\\u003cToolbar /\\\\u003e for displaying the fullscreen button, I discussed with @sfc-gh-bnisco adopting this approach rather than continuing with the `withFullScreenWrapper` higher-order component. After implementation, the result feels much cleaner and more maintainable\u2014thanks, Bob! (You can check out the changes in `AudioInput.tsx` as an example of this migration.)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Why the WidgetLabel Changes?\\\\r\\\\nThe `\\\\u003cToolbar /\\\\u003e` needs a target element to trigger its appearance. Without specifying this, the toolbar would render above the entire container div, which is not ideal. By applying the same strategy used in the toolbar to the WidgetLabel, we can centralize the label logic and importantly prevent the widget label from being included in the returned widget markup (while still keeping this collocated in the widget component).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Next Steps\\\\r\\\\nThis is an early implementation, and I\\'d like to get feedback from the team before proceeding further. Does anyone see any potential issues or limitations with this approach that we might need to address? Let me know your thoughts!\\\\r\\\\n\",\"state\":\"opened\",\"created_at\":\"2024-10-02T20:02:24.000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-04T23:49:32.000Z\",\"merged_by\":null,\"merge_user\":null,\"merged_at\":null,\"closed_by\":null,\"closed_at\":null,\"target_branch\":\"develop\",\"source_branch\":\"nico/shared-toolbar-and-widget-label\",\"user_notes_count\":37,\"upvotes\":0,\"downvotes\":0,\"author\":{\"id\":1,\"username\":\"root\",\"name\":\"Administrator\",\"state\":\"active\",\"locked\":false,\"avatar_url\":\"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/bc780a96456fadbe364f4d9b9ef1276c288db81171546a91d8331887c81b9cf3?s=80\\\\u0026d=identicon\",\"web_url\":\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root\"},\"assignees\":[],\"assignee\":null,\"reviewers\":[],\"source_project_id\":14,\"target_project_id\":14,\"labels\":[],\"draft\":false,\"imported\":true,\"imported_from\":\"gitlab_project\",\"work_in_progress\":false,\"milestone\":null,\"merge_when_pipeline_succeeds\":false,\"merge_status\":\"unchecked\",\"detailed_merge_status\":\"unchecked\",\"merge_after\":null,\"sha\":\"4d32babf5ff0b1b2c7e0575cdd7b860206776536\",\"merge_commit_sha\":null,\"squash_commit_sha\":null,\"discussion_locked\":null,\"should_remove_source_branch\":null,\"force_remove_source_branch\":null,\"prepared_at\":null,\"reference\":\"!9590\",\"references\":{\"short\":\"!9590\",\"relative\":\"!9590\",\"full\":\"root/streamlit!9590\"},\"web_url\":\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/streamlit/-/merge_requests/9590\",\"time_stats\":{\"time_estimate\":0,\"total_time_spent\":0,\"human_time_estimate\":null,\"human_total_time_spent\":null},\"squash\":false,\"squash_on_merge\":false,\"task_completion_status\":{\"count\":0,\"completed_count\":0},\"has_conflicts\":false,\"blocking_discussions_resolved\":true},{\"id\":40492,\"iid\":9588,\"project_id\":14,\"title\":\"Eliminate symlink requirement in component request handler\",\"description\":\"*Created by: kmcgrady*\\\\n\\\\n## Describe your changes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOn first implementation, we were extra stringent and disallowed symlinks in the component path in order to determine whether a URL is valid. It turns out, it\\'s not a strict requirement so long as the original path (once normalized) is still a valid path. Furthermore, use cases have appeared where build systems leverage symbolic links, so valid components are unable to work. So, we will remove this requirement.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Testing Plan\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Removed the python test for symlinks, and kept the relative path test to cover the security issue.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n---\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n**Contribution License Agreement**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBy submitting this pull request you agree that all contributions to this project are made under the Apache 2.0 license.\\\\r\\\\n\",\"state\":\"opened\",\"created_at\":\"2024-10-02T18:52:40.000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-03T17:02:03.000Z\",\"merged_by\":null,\"merge_user\":null,\"merged_at\":null,\"closed_by\":null,\"closed_at\":null,\"target_branch\":\"develop\",\"source_branch\":\"fix/component-symlink\",\"user_notes_count\":1,\"upvotes\":0,\"downvotes\":0,\"author\":{\"id\":1,\"username\":\"root\",\"name\":\"Administrator\",\"state\":\"active\",\"locked\":false,\"avatar_url\":\"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/bc780a96456fadbe364f4d9b9ef1276c288db81171546a91d8331887c81b9cf3?s=80\\\\u0026d=identicon\",\"web_url\":\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root\"},\"assignees\":[],\"assignee\":null,\"reviewers\":[],\"source_project_id\":14,\"target_project_id\":14,\"labels\":[\"chang